 * §7.144 two-year records; §7.145 invoice/contract; §7.123 insurance.
 *
 * Pest facts used, all sourced above in .research/pest-species.md:
 *  - German cockroach: carried in, does NOT live outdoors in Texas; 75% of
 *    life in cracks 1/32-3/16 in; bug bombs do not penetrate; bait placement
 *    within 1-2 ft of harbourage, many small placements; daytime sightings and
 *    dispersal are severity indicators; HEPA vacuum (allergens).
 *  - American cockroach: sewer/drain/soffit/door-threshold wanderer; keep
 *    P-traps filled.
 *  - Rodents: 1/4 in exclusion standard; metal or concrete, not foam/plastic/
 *    wood/rubber/steel wool; thigmotaxis along wall-floor corners; mice within
 *    ~30 ft of nest; traps <=10 ft apart close to walls; mice not neophobic,
 *    rats are; rub marks = rat sign; store 18 in off floor, off walls.
 *  - Stored product insects arrive on incoming freight; cardboard is
